# Web coding style

Matches the spirit of `.cursor/rules/coding-style.mdc` for **presentation code**.

## File organization

Prefer **feature / surface** folders, not “all buttons in one flat folder unless tiny”:

```text
src/
├── components/
│   └── hero/
│       ├── Hero.tsx
│       ├── HeroVisual.tsx
│       └── hero.css
├── hooks/
├── lib/
└── styles/
```

## Design tokens (`:root`)

Centralize palette, type scale, spacing, motion — avoid repeating magic values across components:

```css
:root {
  --color-surface: oklch(98% 0 0);
  --text-base: clamp(1rem, 0.92rem + 0.4vw, 1.125rem);
  --duration-normal: 300ms;
  --ease-out-expo: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
}
```

## Motion

Prefer **`transform`**, **`opacity`**, **`clip-path`** (and **`filter`** sparingly). Avoid animating layout (`width`, `height`, top/left, margin, padding, border-width, `font-size`) when it triggers reflow unless there is no alternative.

## Semantic HTML

Use **`header` / `nav` / `main` / `section` / `footer`**, headings with stable **`id`** for **`aria-labelledby`**, landmarks + labels — not infinite anonymous **`div`** shells.

## Naming

- Components: **PascalCase**
- Hooks: **`use*`**
- CSS: **kebab-case** or utilities per project convention
- Animation helpers: camelCase + intent (**`heroRevealTl`**)